      "The classic developer mistake is handing subsystems to different contractors. One crew does CCTV, another the fire alarm, a third the network. Each has its own design, its own tray, its own schedule and its own idea of where the other's responsibility ends. Routes get duplicated, timelines stack instead of running in parallel — and at handover, when the fire signal must release the access-controlled doors, it turns out the two systems have never met.",
