      "Surveillance systems differ by more than camera count. An IP system gives high resolution, single-cable power (PoE) and precise analytics but needs a proper network; analog HDCVI/TVI is cheaper and runs over existing coax, so it is the choice when upgrading an older site. Wireless cameras help where cable cannot go, but depend on Wi-Fi quality and power. On most sites we build a mixed scheme: IP where facial and plate detail matters, analog on the perimeter and in utility areas.",
